@baseUrl = https://localhost:7030
@tenant = root
@targetTenant = acme

### 0. Sign in as a root operator (the exchange is root-only)
# @name operatorToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/{{tenant}}/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@root.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 1. Exchange the operator token for one that acts inside {{targetTenant}}
# ADR-0002: root operators cross tenants by exchanging tokens, never by header. The issued token's
# `tenant` claim is the target and its subject is a real user of that tenant (targetUserId, else
# the tenant's admin), so permissions there work unchanged. Access-only: no refresh token, no
# cookie, no session row. A longer duration than the server's maximum is clamped, not refused.
# @name exchange
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/operator/token-exchange
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "targetTenantId": "{{targetTenant}}",
  "targetUserId": null,
  "reason": "Customer ticket #4821 — verifying their branding",
  "durationMinutes": 15
}

### 2. Use the exchanged token — this lists {{targetTenant}}'s users, not root's
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{exchange.response.body.accessToken}}

### 3. A forged tenant header changes nothing (the claim is the only input)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/users
Authorization: Bearer {{exchange.response.body.accessToken}}
tenant: root

### 4. Read + write the target tenant's branding while acting
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/tenants/theme
Authorization: Bearer {{exchange.response.body.accessToken}}

### 5. Exit the tenant — ends the grant, returns no token
# The operator's own session was never touched, so there is nothing to restore: the client simply
# stops sending the exchanged token, which is dead from here on.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonation/end
Authorization: Bearer {{exchange.response.body.accessToken}}

### 6. Or revoke the grant from the operator side (same effect, different door)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonation/grants/{{exchange.response.body.grantId}}/revoke
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "reason": "done for the day"
}

### 7. The exchange appears in the unified grant list
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonation/grants?Status=Active&ImpersonatedTenantId={{targetTenant}}
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken.response.body.accessToken}}

### 8. Same-tenant impersonation (NOT cross-tenant — that is the exchange above)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/identity/impersonation/start
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{operatorToken.response.body.accessToken}}

{
  "targetUserId": "<a user in YOUR OWN tenant>",
  "targetTenantId": "{{tenant}}",
  "reason": "reproducing a support ticket",
  "durationMinutes": 15
}
